{"authored" [{"question" "q-50222" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5ffccc056d43c528012bcb9c43d0684d0799657c1a2679280b6a6fed57beb94" "basis" 1160 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50222" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to use integration by parts. \n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2})(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5ffccc056d43c528012bcb9c43d0684d0799657c1a2679280b6a6fed57beb94" "basis" 1160 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012723/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50222" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012